==English==
{{was wotd|2007|May|23}}

===Alternative forms===
{{alter|en|Linnean|Linean|Linnæan|Linæan}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|Linnaeus|an}}. After {{w|lang=en|Carl Linnaeus|Carolus Linnaeus}} (1707–1778), Swedish naturalist who helped to standardize biological nomenclature.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/lɪˈneɪ.ən/|/lɪˈniː.ən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Linnaean.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Linnaean-2.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪən|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|biology}} Of or relating to {{w|Carolus Linnaeus}}, [[Swedish]] [[naturalist]], either personally or in a wider sense, to the era influenced by him.
# {{lb|en|taxonomy}} Of or relating to the [[binomial]] [[nomenclature]] originated by him
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Daniel R. Headrick|title=When Information Came of Age|page=26|text=Nowhere was the victory of Linnaeanism more complete than in Britain. When William Hudson's ''Flora Anglica'', organized in the '''Linnaean''' manner, appeared in 1762, it displaced all previous floras.}}
# Relating to the nomenclature ''Codes'' that have their starting point in a work by Linnaeus or are derived from such a ''Code''. This includes the idea of a ranked taxonomy, which was not initiated by Linnaeus.

